.TH SPARKLINK.CONF 5 "2025-04-05" "SparkLink" "File Formats Manual"
.SH NAME
sparklink.conf \- SparkLink daemon configuration file
.SH SYNOPSIS
.I /etc/sparklink/main.conf
.SH DESCRIPTION
This file controls the runtime behaviour of
.BR slkd (8).
It uses TOML syntax.
.PP
Only a missing implicit default file permits built\-in defaults. An explicitly
supplied path must exist, including when it equals the default location. Read,
permission, parsing, unknown-field and unsupported-policy errors abort startup
before D\-Bus registration or controller management ownership.
.SH SECTIONS
.SS [general]
.TP
.B discovery_level
Integer 0\(en4. Minimum discovery level filter for scan results.
This filter is used by the legacy scan path. Native WS73 currently requires
level 1; another configured level is rejected for that adapter before acquiring
its management lease. Default:
.BR 1 .
.TP
.B auto_enable
Boolean. Currently only true is supported; false is rejected until controller
enable policy is implemented. Default:
.BR true .
.TP
.B name
String. Daemon adapter alias; does not set the native radio advertisement name. Default:
.BR \(dqSparkLink\(dq .
.SS [policy]
.TP
.B auto_pair
Boolean. Currently only false is supported. True is rejected because authenticated
automatic pairing is not implemented. Default:
.BR false .
.TP
.B min_encryption
Integer. Currently only 0 is supported. Nonzero values are rejected until
per-connection encryption enforcement is implemented. This setting is not a
claim of authenticated or encrypted connection support. Default:
.BR 0 .
.SH EXAMPLE
.nf
[general]
discovery_level = 1
auto_enable = true
name = "Living Room Hub"

[policy]
auto_pair = false
min_encryption = 0
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/sparklink/main.conf
Default location loaded by
.BR slkd (8).
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR slkd (8),
.BR slctl (1)
